DESCRIPTION:Ali Sultan saw his first stand-up comedian after moving to Amer
 ica from Yemen at the age of 15. He developed a desire to go on stage\, but
  first\, he to learn English.\n\nAli became the first Yemeni-Ethiopian Amer
 ican to make a stand-up television network debut on The Late Show with Step
 hen Colbert. He has appeared on Comedy Central’s Hart of the City with Ke
 vin Hart and filmed his half-hour comedy special in Dubai for Comedy Centra
 l Arabia. He has also been featured on Don’t Tell Comedy and Comics Unlea
 shed. He also represented Minnesota and won the Best in the Midwest competi
 tion at Gilda’s LaughFest.\n\nHis albums Happy to Be Here and Funny First
  can be heard on Spotify\, and have garnered over one million streams on Pa
 ndora. His latest special from Dry Bar Comedy has received 1.8 million view
 s on YouTube.\n\nPlease note\, there is a 2 item per person minimum in the 
 showroom. This can be any combination of food items or beverages. This does
  NOT include items bought in the basement at the Bier Baron Tavern.\n\nAll 
 General Admission seating is first come first serve\, therefore we cannot g
 uarantee seating together. Groups need to be particularly aware of this. We
  recommend arriving at least 30 minutes to an hour prior to show time for b
 etter seat selection.\n\nDoors close 30 minutes after showtime.\n\nTickets 
 are available at the door UNLESS tickets have sold out.\n\nGuests must be 1
 8+for entry. Those under the age of 21 will be given wristbands to wear.\n\
 nALL SALES ARE FINAL. NO REFUNDS. This includes switching of showtimes\, on
 ce purchased all sales are final.\n\nManagement reserves the right to preve
 nt customers from entering the facility who they deem disruptive or dangero
 us to other patrons.\n\nWe offer sign language interpretation upon request.
